+# Run the experimental room journey locally
+
+`run-spawn-room-localnet.mjs` runs a fresh local validator, Photon, ring indexer,
+the application prover, and RingRPC with the pinned in-memory local KMS. It then
+runs the TypeScript create → advance → recover → reuse journey and stops the
+processes it owns. Services and tests share one parent process, which also works
+in executors that isolate the loopback network between separate commands.
+
+This profile uses the two explicitly generated local proving keys. The runner
+does not create proving keys, download dependencies, or call a hosted Solana
+RPC. It does not change the upstream baseline source or deploy remotely.
+
+## Prerequisites
+
+Use the Go version in `prover/go.mod`, the Rust toolchain in
+`rust-toolchain.toml`, and SBF platform tools v1.54. Install the native compiler
+dependencies required by the pinned upstream checkout. On smaller machines,
+build with `CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=1`, `CARGO_PROFILE_DEV_DEBUG=0`, and
+`CARGO_PROFILE_TEST_DEBUG=0`.
+
+Keep a separate clean native checkout at custom-rings commit
+`02bca33729051798834ecbb4d94e968cdc0ef9b8`, with its Zolana submodule at
+`0fe4f952182b39464d472c52c40b3febe6cbd9ec`. In that checkout, build the native
+prerequisites and fetch the custom-ring catalog:
+
+```sh
+JUST_NO_DOTENV=true just build-programs build-localnet-tools fetch-custom-ring-keys
+```
+
+The native cache needs `transfer_ring_2_2.key` for genesis (included by the
+custom-ring fetch command), plus `transfer_eddsa_ring_1_2.key` and
+`transfer_eddsa_ring_2_2.key` for the hidden-owner rail. Fetch exactly the required
+extra keys with the pinned recipe, which verifies their hashes and sizes:
+
+```sh
+RING_EXTRA_SPP_KEY='transfer_eddsa_ring_1_2.key transfer_eddsa_ring_2_2.key' \
+  JUST_NO_DOTENV=true just fetch-custom-ring-keys
+```
+
+The runner independently checks the SHA256 and size of every cached native key
+against the two pinned lockfiles before serving any keys. It does not fetch the
+full SPP catalog.
+
+In this application checkout, install the pinned npm dependencies, prepare the
+application keys/program/prover with `tools/prepare-spawn-room-localnet.sh`, and
+install the pinned npm dependencies in the sibling `backroom-rings/backrooms`
+directory. That clean checkout must be at Backrooms commit
+`08822c65254cd73c5f2dccbdf182ce1df2c7510a`. The journey imports its real
+`reference-host` and Flue source; the runner verifies the revision and clean
+status before and after the run.
+
+The application preparation command is expensive on its first run. It creates
+the two separate experimental keys, runs their full proof tests, exports the
+matching verification keys and public proof vectors, and builds the explicit
+localnet application profile. Preserve its ignored `target/spawn-room-keys`
+directory between runs. Never substitute these keys or the app SBF artifact for
+the upstream baseline catalog or program.
+
+## One command for services and journey
+
+Create a JSON config outside tracked source, using absolute paths:
+
+```json
+{
+  "disposableLocalnet": true,
+  "nativeRepo": "/path/to/clean/custom-rings",
+  "referenceHostRoot": "/path/to/backroom-rings/backrooms/reference-host",
+  "binaries": {
+    "surfpool": "/path/to/surfpool",
+    "solana": "/path/to/solana",
+    "solanaKeygen": "/path/to/solana-keygen"
+  }
+}
+```
+
+Then run:
+
+```sh
+node tools/run-spawn-room-localnet.mjs --config /absolute/path/to/localnet-run.json
+```
+
+The default app program ID is
+`2t8SPCrLAxKjhYjY1Yy1Dwx2ktRaKZ6fGf5khcY5zb5Y`. The default artifact is
+`target/deploy/custom_ring_program.so`, and the default prover is
+`target/spawn-room-prover`. Native binaries are taken from the clean checkout's
+`target/debug` or `zolana/target/debug`. Every executable can be supplied under
+`binaries`: `zolana`, `xtask`, `photon`, `ringIndexer`, `ringRpc`, `prover`,
+`surfpool`, `solana`, `solanaKeygen`, and `npm`.
+
+Other optional config fields are `programId`, `programSo`,
+`applicationKeysDirectory`, `nativeKeysDirectory`, `workParent`, and `ports`.
+The default application key directory is `target/spawn-room-keys`; native keys
+default to the clean checkout's `zolana/prover/server/proving-keys`. No large
+keys are copied: the fresh served-key directory contains symlinks to validated
+immutable artifacts.
+
+| Service | Default port |
+| --- | ---: |
+| Validator RPC | 42899 |
+| Validator websocket / auxiliary | 42900 / 42901 |
+| Photon | 42784 |
+| Ring indexer | 42786 |
+| RingRPC | 42785 |
+| Application prover | 45001 |
+| Prover metrics | 51998 |
+
+All client URLs and configurable service binds use loopback. The pinned Photon
+binary hardcodes its API listener to `0.0.0.0` and has no bind option; run this
+profile inside an isolated runtime without publishing that port. The receipt
+records this inherited limitation. The local KMS takes a free loopback port.
+An occupied port is a failure; the runner never kills another service to
+take its port. It generates fresh upgrade-authority, fee-payer, and publisher
+keypairs, and funds them only through its own validator's airdrop endpoint.
+The journey creates its records registry, ring configuration, enrollment,
+application state, and native encrypted records using the supplied local
+configuration.
+
+## Evidence and failure handling
+
+Each run creates a new private `target/spawn-room-runs/journey-*` directory and
+prints its path immediately. The directory contains:
+
+- `run-receipt.json`: started/completed commands, artifact and key hashes,
+  tracked and untracked source manifests, reference-host identity, resource
+  settings, measured command durations, scope-labeled sampled process RSS and
+  OS high-water marks, service ownership, cleanup status, and the final result.
+- `journey-evidence.json`: the actual journey's named checks and transaction
+  signatures, written by the TypeScript test.
+- `vitest-results.json`: the test runner's machine-readable result.
+- Private service logs, fresh local keypairs, local databases, and account
+  snapshots. Do not commit the whole directory.
+
+A run passes only when Vitest executes at least one passing test with no skips,
+the journey reports passed `create`, `advance`, `recovery`, and `reuse` steps,
+owned services stop successfully, and implementation sources remain unchanged
+during the run. A running receipt after an interrupted
+executor is incomplete evidence, not a pass. An unsuccessful run retains its
+logs for diagnosis and a fresh command creates a new isolated run directory.
+These application receipts are separate from the upstream CR01 baseline.
+
+Resource measurements cover only the harness, its service/command process
+groups, and observed descendants. They exclude unrelated build and Go test
+lanes. The receipt distinguishes sampled concurrent RSS from each process's
+observed OS high-water mark, records the sampling interval and limitations, and
+keeps configured heap limits separate. The native workers also record their
+own process high-water marks before exiting. These are local-run measurements.
+
+The lightweight runner checks can be repeated without starting services:
+
+```sh
+node --test tools/run-spawn-room-localnet.test.mjs
+```
